  "raw_response": "```json\n{\n  \"modifications\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Introduce a phosphate ester group to improve solubility and serve as a prodrug that can be cleaved enzymatically to release the active drug.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"CC1(C2CC2NC(=O)C(F)(F)F)CN1C(=O)C(NC(=O)C1CC1(C#N)COP(=O)(O)O)C(C)(C)C\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Phosphate esters are commonly used in prodrugs to enhance aqueous solubility and improve absorption while being cleaved by phosphatases in vivo to release the active drug.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Add an L-valine ester group to the nitrile-bearing cyclopropane to improve oral bioavailability by leveraging peptide transporter-mediated uptake.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"CC1(C2CC2NC(=O)C(F)(F)F)CN1C(=O)C(NC(=O)C1CC1(COC(=O)C(C)N)C)C(C)(C)C\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Valine esters can exploit the natural peptide transport systems in the gut, improving absorption and oral bioavailability.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Attach a methyl succinate group to the primary amide to enhance prodrug properties and allow enzymatic cleavage to release the active drug.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"CC1(C2CC2NC(=O)C(F)(F)F)CN1C(=O)C(NC(=O)C1CC1(C#N)C(=O)OCC(=O)OC)C(C)(C)C\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Methyl succinate esters are known to improve hydrophilicity and serve as effective ester prodrugs that are metabolized to release the active compound in vivo.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
